      "side": 1,
      "message": "`existing_by_mac` is built once and the create path never checks `name`, so two cases still duplicate. Reproduced: the same MAC learned on two ports in one scan creates two interfaces with that MAC, and a NIC swap (new MAC on a port whose LLDP port-id is still `em1`) creates a second `em1` beside the existing one. The create route enforces no uniqueness, and `delete_interface` drops the first name match, so a duplicate name makes `--rm-interface` ambiguous. Tracking created names/MACs in a set and skipping with a warning closes it.",
      "revId": "0a9a52aca62dbed06709e7fa5020b24d351166a3",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
