      "side": 1,
      "message": "`_parse_fdb` strips the logical unit at line 77 but this key keeps it, so on Junos that print `ge-0/0/0.0` in `show lldp neighbors` the neighbor keys never match the FDB\u0027s `ge-0/0/0`. Every row then comes back with `neighbor\u003dNone` and `name\u003dNone`: the report loses the names and `--apply` matches nothing for any host. A unit-suffixed fixture reproduces it (`No LLDP-identified NICs matched host ...`, zero creates). Keying on `tokens[0].split(\".\")[0]` aligns it with the FDB.",
